   "source": [
    "# Create/convert an input dataset in MRD format\n",
    "\n",
    "Prepare a dataset in the [MRD file format](https://ismrmrd.readthedocs.io/en/latest/mrd_files.html) by converting acquired data or by generating a synthetic phantom dataset.  Raw k-space data can be converted using tools such as [siemens_to_ismrmrd](https://github.com/ismrmrd/siemens_to_ismrmrd), [ge_to_ismrmrd](https://github.com/ismrmrd/ge_to_ismrmrd), [philips_to_ismrmrd](https://github.com/ismrmrd/philips_to_ismrmrd), and [bruker_to_ismrmrd](https://github.com/ismrmrd/bruker_to_ismrmrd), while DICOM image data can be converted to DICOM using [dicom2mrd.py](https://github.com/kspaceKelvin/python-ismrmrd-server#UsingDICOMimagesasinputdata).  The [generate_cartesian_shepp_logan_dataset.py](../generate_cartesian_shepp_logan_dataset.py) script can also be used to generate multi-channel raw k-space data.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Option 1: Simulate a raw k-space dataset of the Shepp-Logan phantom\n",
    "**Note** This section requires that the [ismrmrd-python-tools](https://github.com/ismrmrd/ismrmrd-python-tools) repo be installed (see [readme.md](../readme.md#Settingupacondaenvironment))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Creating Shepp-Logan phantom raw data:\n",
      "Matrix 256x256 at R=1 with 1 repetitions\n",
      "8 coils with 2 oversampling and 0.05 noise level\n",
      "Saved to data/raw.mrd\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Generate a raw k-space dataset of the Shepp-Logan phantom\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import generate_cartesian_shepp_logan_dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "inputFilename = 'data/raw.mrd'\n",
    "\n",
    "dir, file = os.path.split(inputFilename)\n",
    "if dir and not os.path.exists(dir):\n",
    "    print(f'Creating parent directory {dir}')\n",
    "    os.makedirs(dir)\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(inputFilename):\n",
    "    overwrite = input(f'File {inputFilename} already exists!  Overwrite? y/[n]')\n",
    "    if overwrite.lower() == 'y':\n",
    "        os.remove(inputFilename)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        raise Exception('Aborting to not overwrite existing file')\n",
    "\n",
    "generate_cartesian_shepp_logan_dataset.create(filename=inputFilename, matrix_size=256, coils=8, oversampling=2, repetitions=1, acceleration=1, noise_level=0.05)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Option 2: Convert raw k-space data acquired from an MRI scanner"
